          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em defect brane
            (
            %a{:href => "#BershoeffOrtinRiccioni11"}> Bershoeff-Ortin-Riccioni 11
            ) is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane"} brane
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codimension"} codimension
            2 (hence an “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exotic+brane"}> exotic brane
            ”); such as, for example
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosmic+string"} cosmic string
                in 4-dimensional
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+theory"} Yang-Mills theory
            %li
              %p
                a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+1-brane+in+4d"} super 1-brane in 4d
            %li
              %p
                a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+2-brane+in+5d"} super 2-brane in 5d
            %li
              %p
                a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+3-brane+in+6d"} super 3-brane in 6d
            %li
              %p
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D7-brane"} D7-brane
                in 10d
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+IIB+string+theory"} type IIB string theory
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/U-duality"} U-duality
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monodromy"} monodromy
            have been argued to be identified with “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exotic+branes"}> exotic branes
            ”
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#deBoerShigemori12"} deBoer &amp; Shigemori 2012, p. 12
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#RelationToAnyons Relation to anyons
          %p
            An
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anyon"} anyon
            is traditionally realized as a point-particle/defect in 2+1-dimensional spacetime, hence as a codimension-2 “0-brane” (see the references
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "braid+group+statistics#ReferencesVortexAnyons"} here
            %a{:href => "#deBoerShigemori12"} deBoer &amp; Shigemori 2012, p. 65
            and further developed in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#SS22"} SS22
          %p
            Concrete implementation of anyonic defect
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strings"} strings
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/4d+TQFT"} 4d TQFT
            is discussed in
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#BaezWiseCrans06"} Baez, Wise &amp; Crans 2006
            %a{:href => "#BullivantMartinsMartin18"} Bullivant, Martins &amp; Martin 2018
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#KongTianZhang20"} Kong, Tian &amp; Zhang 2020, Sec. 2.2
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+braid+group"}> loop braid group
                \-statistics
            = succeed "-statistics" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braid+group"} braid group
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vortex+string"} vortex string
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+brane"} black brane
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exotic+brane"} exotic brane
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domain+wall"} domain wall
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monopole"} monopole
          %h2#references References
          %p
            Branes of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codimension"} codimension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≤
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \leq 2
            are called
            %em non-standard branes
            in:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eric+A.+Bergshoeff"}> Eric A. Bergshoeff
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fabio+Riccioni"} Fabio Riccioni
              = succeed "," do
                %em Solitonic branes and wrapping rules
              %strong 43
              (2012) 557–561 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1134/S106377961205005X"}> doi:10.1134/S106377961205005X
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Claudia+de+Rham"}> Claudia de Rham
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The Effective Field Theory of Codimension-two Branes
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0707.0884"} arXiv:0707.0884
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1088/1126-6708/2008/01/060"} doi:10.1088/1126-6708/2008/01/060
          %p The term “defect brane” was introduced in:
          %ul
            %li#BershoeffOrtinRiccioni11
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eric+Bergshoeff"}> Eric Bergshoeff
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tomas+Ortin"} Tomas Ortin
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fabio+Riccioni"} Fabio Riccioni
              = succeed "," do
                %em Defect Branes
              %strong 856
              2 (2012) 210-227 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1109.4484"}> arXiv:1109.4484
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2011.10.037"} doi:10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2011.10.037
          %p
            Identification of codimension-2 defect branes with
            = succeed "-group" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/U-duality"} U-duality
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monodromy"} monodromy
            as
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exotic+branes"} exotic branes
          %ul
            %li#deBoerShigemori12
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jan+de+Boer"}> Jan de Boer
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Masaki+Shigemori"} Masaki Shigemori
              = succeed "," do
                %em Exotic Branes in String Theory
              %strong 532
              (2013) 65-118 (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1209.6056"}> arXiv:1209.6056
              ,
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.physrep.2013.07.003"} doi:j.physrep.2013.07.003
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Allan Bayntun, C.P. Burgess, Leo van Nierop,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Codimension-2 Brane-Bulk Matching: Examples from Six and Ten Dimensions
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0912.3039"} arXiv:0912.3039
            %li
              %p
                Takashi Okada, Yuho Sakatani,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Defect branes as Alice strings
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1411.1043"} arXiv:1411.1043
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/JHEP03(2015)131"} doi:10.1007/JHEP03(2015)131
            %li
              %p
                Yosuke Imamura, Hirotaka Kato,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Codimension-2 brane solutions of maximal supergravities in 9, 8, and 7 dimensions
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1711.03242"} arXiv:1711.03242
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1093/ptep/pty045"} doi:10.1093/ptep/pty045
          %p
            Discussion of defect
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28p%2Cq%295-branes"} (p,q)5-branes
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tetsuji+Kimura"}> Tetsuji Kimura
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Defect
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi p
                          %mo ,
                          %mi q
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (p,q)
                    Five-branes
                %strong 893
                (2015) 1-20 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1410.8403"}> arXiv:1410.8403
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2015.01.023"} doi:10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2015.01.023
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tetsuji+Kimura"}> Tetsuji Kimura
                , Shin Sasaki, Kenta Shiozawa,
                %em On Geometries and Monodromies for Branes of Codimension Two
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2312.03358"}> arXiv:2312.03358
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Discussion of codimension-2 defects in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-brane"} M5-brane
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/little+string+theory"} little string theory
            (cf.
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/3-brane+in+6d"} 3-brane in 6d
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hironori+Mori"}> Hironori Mori
                , Yuji Sugimoto, around Fig. 9 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Surface Operators from M-strings
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1608.02849"} arXiv:1608.02849
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevD.95.026001"} doi:10.1103/PhysRevD.95.026001
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hironori+Mori"}> Hironori Mori
                ,
                %em M-theory Perspectives on Codimension-2 Defects
                (
                %a{:href => "https://inspirehep.net/literature/1519095"}> spire:1519095
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www2.yukawa.kyoto-u.ac.jp/~soken.editorial/shuron/DoctoralThesis_Mori.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                Nathan Haouzi, Christian Schmid,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Little String Origin of Surface Defects
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1608.07279"} arXiv:1608.07279
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/JHEP05(2017)082"} doi:10.1007/JHEP05(2017)082
            %li
              %p
                Pietro Capuozzo, John Estes, Brandon Robinson, Benjamin Suzzoni,
                %em Holographic Weyl Anomalies for 4d Defects in 6d SCFTs
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2310.17447"}> arXiv:2310.17447
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            and in relation to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+Seiberg-Witten+curves"} quantum Seiberg-Witten curves
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/class+S-theories"} class S-theories
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jin+Chen"}> Jin Chen
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Babak+Haghighat"} Babak Haghighat
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hee-Cheol+Kim"} Hee-Cheol Kim
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marcus+Sperling"} Marcus Sperling
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Elliptic Quantum Curves of Class
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝒮
                          %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}_k
              %strong 2021
              28 (2021) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2008.05155"}> arXiv:2008.05155
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/JHEP03(2021)028"} doi:10.1007/JHEP03(2021)028
          %p
            and in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D5+supergravity"} D=5 supergravity
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Minkyu Park,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Masaki+Shigemori"} Masaki Shigemori
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Codimension-2 Solutions in Five-Dimensional Supergravity
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1505.05169"} arXiv:1505.05169
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Masaki+Shigemori"}> Masaki Shigemori
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Interpolating between multi-center microstate geometries
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2105.11639"} arXiv:2105.11639
          %p
            On defect strings in 4d
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/TQFT"} TQFT
            satisfying
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braid+group"} braid group
            = succeed "-statistics:" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+braid+group"} loop braid group
          %p
            in 4d
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BF+theory"} BF theory
          %ul
            %li#BaezWiseCrans06
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"}> John Baez
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Derek+Wise"} Derek Wise
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alissa+Crans"} Alissa Crans
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Exotic Statistics for Strings in 4d BF Theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/gr-qc/0603085"} arXiv:gr-qc/0603085
            %li#BullivantMartinsMartin18
              %p
                Alex Bullivant,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jo%C3%A3o+Faria+Martins"} João Faria Martins
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Representations of the Loop Braid Group and Aharonov-Bohm like effects in discrete (3+1)-dimensional higher gauge theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1807.09551"} arXiv:1807.09551
          %p
            and in the
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/3d+toric+code"} 3d toric code
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/4d+TQFT"} 4d TQFT
          %ul
            %li#KongTianZhang20
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Liang+Kong"}> Liang Kong
              , Yin Tian, Zhi-Hao Zhang, Section 2.2 of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Defects in the 3-dimensional toric code model form a braided fusion 2-category
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2009.06564"} arXiv:2009.06564
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/JHEP12(2020)078"} doi:10.1007/JHEP12(2020)078
          %p
            Incorporation of defect branes into the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory+classification+of+D-brane+charge"} K-theory classification of D-brane charge
            by understanding the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypergeometric+construction+of+KZ+solutions"} hypergeometric construction of KZ solutions
            as happening in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+equivariant+differential+K-theory"} twisted equivariant differential K-theory
          %ul
            %li#SS22
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"}> Hisham Sati
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Anyonic+defect+branes+in+TED-K-theory"} Anyonic defect branes in TED-K-theory
              %strong 35
              06 (2023) 2350009 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2203.11838"}> arXiv:2203.11838
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/S0129055X23500095"} doi:10.1142/S0129055X23500095
          %p
            On defect branes in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D4+N%3D4+SYM"} D=4 N=4 SYM
            via
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS%2FCFT"} AdS/CFT
          %ul
            %li
              Hongliang Jiang,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Arkady+A.+Tseytlin"} Arkady A. Tseytlin
              %em
                On co-dimension 2 defect anomalies in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒩
                      %mo =
                      %mn 4
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{N}=4
                SYM and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (2,0)
                theory via brane probes in AdS/CFT
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2402.07881"}> arXiv:2402.07881
              \&amp;rbrack;
        .revisedby
